  grammarNotes: [
    { sentence: "While television cooking competitions are often thought of as a high-stakes, life-changing experience that can make your career, they often don't, and contestants say that much of the industry success they've had in the notoriously competitive and fickle food world is the result of their own hustling and hard work.", explanation: "While 引导让步状语从句（虽然……），从句内 that can make your career 为定语从句修饰 experience。主句由 and 连接两个并列分句：they often don't（省略了 make your career）与 contestants say that...。say 后为 that 宾语从句，从句主干为 much of the industry success is the result of...，其中 they've had... 为省略关系词的定语从句修饰 success。" },
    { sentence: "Tasha Oren, director of film and media studies at Tufts University and author of the new book Food TV, which examines how culinary culture became part of pop culture, said that television appearances can strengthen a professional chef's branding and public relations, but that the experience is often different for non-professional chefs who may be expecting to find an industry career after being on the small screen.", explanation: "主干为 Tasha Oren said that... but that...。主语后接两个并列同位语（director... and author...）说明身份；which examines... 为非限定性定语从句修饰 Food TV。谓语 said 后接两个并列的 that 宾语从句（can strengthen... but that the experience is often different...）；第二个从句中 who may be expecting... 为定语从句修饰 non-professional chefs，after being on the small screen 为介词+动名词作时间状语。" },
    { sentence: "The TV personality said that hit shows, which have a built-in audience that's loyal and dedicated, can certainly help contestants in their offscreen careers thanks to the shows' reach.", explanation: "主干为 The TV personality said that...。that 宾语从句主干为 hit shows can help contestants；which have a built-in audience 为非限定性定语从句修饰 hit shows，其中 that's loyal and dedicated 为定语从句修饰 audience；thanks to the shows' reach 为介词短语作原因状语。" }
  ],
  quiz: [
    { question: "What did Palak Patel mean by saying her wins were 'a story of grit rather than one of overnight stardom'?", options: ["Winning the competitions immediately made her famous", "Her success came from persistence and hard work, not instant fame", "She won because she had 17 agents supporting her", "TV competitions made her career with no extra effort"], correctAnswer: 1, explanation: "P1、P5 表明：胜利并未立刻改变生活，参赛者认为成功主要靠自己的拼搏（hustling and hard work），电视竞赛履历是坚韧的故事而非一夜成名。B 正确；A、C、D 与原文相反。" },
    { question: "According to Tasha Oren, what can TV do for a chef?", options: ["It can turn anyone into a great cook", "It can amplify a story the chef already has, but cannot improve their skill", "It guarantees an industry career for non-professional chefs", "It replaces the need for branding and public relations"], correctAnswer: 1, explanation: "P10 奥伦原话：TV can only help in amplifying a story you have, it can't help amplify your skill，即电视只能放大已有故事、无法提升技能。故选 B；其余选项均与原文不符。" },
    { question: "What is the main idea of the article?", options: ["TV cooking competitions offer guaranteed success and high pay", "Winning a cooking show rarely translates into automatic industry success; contestants must hustle and build their own brands", "Only professional chefs should appear on cooking shows", "Reality TV pays contestants generously in royalties"], correctAnswer: 1, explanation: "全文通过帕特尔、奥伦和汗的经历论证：赢得比赛不等于行业成功，参赛者需自己拼搏、经营品牌，且报酬极低（P1、P7-8、P11-13）。B 概括了主旨；A、D 与原文相反，C 未提及。" }
  ]
